1
00:00:05,831 --> 00:00:07,365
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,390 --> 00:00:08,923
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:11,164 --> 00:00:12,864
(Episode 18)

4
00:00:19,577 --> 00:00:20,931
Let's stop here.

5
00:00:22,531 --> 00:00:27,431
They say you don't walk a road
whose end you can see.

6
00:00:28,464 --> 00:00:30,864
I couldn't have gone all the way anyway,

7
00:00:32,764 --> 00:00:36,031
and as a coward
without even that much courage,

8
00:00:38,331 --> 00:00:40,589
if I confused you and shook you,

9
00:00:44,131 --> 00:00:48,831
I'm so sorry for that too.

10
00:00:58,131 --> 00:00:59,831
I have to see the end of it, Gyu Rim.

11
00:01:03,231 --> 00:01:08,231
Even if I get hurt, and you get hurt,
and someone else gets a little hurt,

12
00:01:08,464 --> 00:01:13,531
I have to see where we end up.

13
00:01:33,531 --> 00:01:34,564
Mom.

14
00:01:38,931 --> 00:01:42,101
- Mom.
- Yes, sweetheart.

15
00:01:42,231 --> 00:01:44,442
I hung up all the runaway apology kits.

16
00:01:44,764 --> 00:01:49,031
I wasn't going to put one
on Gyu Yeong's door, but I did anyway.

17
00:01:49,731 --> 00:01:54,234
Good job. What a brave little man you are.

18
00:01:55,064 --> 00:01:56,764
Well done, baby.

19
00:02:00,031 --> 00:02:03,031
Hey, what is this?

20
00:02:03,131 --> 00:02:04,631
It's a runaway apology kit.

21
00:02:04,631 --> 00:02:06,331
Hey, what's that?

22
00:02:06,931 --> 00:02:08,864
A kit to apologize for running away.

23
00:02:09,031 --> 00:02:11,664
So they're errand coupons.

24
00:02:11,964 --> 00:02:14,806
Hey, so I can make you
run errands with these?

25
00:02:14,831 --> 00:02:18,631
Yes. You can ask for a back rub
or have me shine your shoes.

26
00:02:18,764 --> 00:02:20,831
Hey, then give me one more.

27
00:02:20,831 --> 00:02:23,499
No. One kit per person.

28
00:02:23,931 --> 00:02:26,641
Hey, one is a little stingy.

29
00:02:26,731 --> 00:02:28,131
Giving just one will still get you grief.

30
00:02:28,164 --> 00:02:30,531
I'll give you my gummies, Dad.

31
00:02:32,031 --> 00:02:34,541
You can have all my gummies,

32
00:02:35,464 --> 00:02:39,331
so I'm confiscating the errand coupons.

33
00:02:39,731 --> 00:02:43,464
What have we done to earn the right
to exploit a child like this?

34
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:46,731
Honestly...

35
00:02:46,831 --> 00:02:50,731
I'll take this and return
the errand coupons too.

36
00:02:52,031 --> 00:02:54,831
Hey, if you two do this,
what does that make me?

37
00:02:54,864 --> 00:02:59,631
It's fine, Dad. You just go on being
a consistently childish grandfather.

38
00:02:59,731 --> 00:03:03,164
What? You little...

39
00:03:03,437 --> 00:03:04,897
You look fine, though.

40
00:03:05,117 --> 00:03:08,397
I thought your mom would squeeze you
until you popped.

41
00:03:09,231 --> 00:03:12,118
I almost did, but he was too cute to pop.

42
00:03:13,031 --> 00:03:19,231
Then I get to squeeze you until you pop.

43
00:03:19,231 --> 00:03:22,846
- Then I get to tickle you.
- Quiet down!

44
00:03:23,931 --> 00:03:27,593
What is this uneasy feeling
that I'm the only one left out?

45
00:03:28,404 --> 00:03:31,204
Today's special, so let's eat together.

46
00:03:31,731 --> 00:03:33,064
- Yeah?
- Hayashi rice sound good?

47
00:03:33,131 --> 00:03:34,131
- Yes.
- Yes.

48
00:03:34,131 --> 00:03:36,231
- I'd rather have black bean rice.
- Hold on.

49
00:03:36,664 --> 00:03:37,831
Why? What is it?

50
00:03:42,064 --> 00:03:43,364
Why? What is it?

51
00:03:43,564 --> 00:03:44,964
It's Mu Jin.

52
00:03:46,953 --> 00:03:50,931
Mom, Mu Jin says he pulled
a rare Powerball card,

53
00:03:50,964 --> 00:03:53,231
and he's leaving it in the milk holder.

54
00:03:53,531 --> 00:03:56,631
Hey, who is this Mu Jin?

55
00:03:56,664 --> 00:03:58,864
A man Mom and I both like a lot.

56
00:04:03,764 --> 00:04:06,564
A man? A grown man?

57
00:04:26,664 --> 00:04:28,893
- Mu Jin.
- Gyeol.

58
00:04:29,331 --> 00:04:32,635
You really pulled a rare Powerball card?

59
00:04:32,956 --> 00:04:33,956
Take a look.

60
00:04:38,031 --> 00:04:39,119
It's real.

61
00:04:42,230 --> 00:04:46,772
Hey, you. Hold on a second.

62
00:04:50,631 --> 00:04:55,064
I know that face from somewhere.

63
00:04:55,331 --> 00:04:58,631
Yes. It's been a while, sir.

64
00:04:59,043 --> 00:05:01,710
Sir? You...

65
00:05:08,314 --> 00:05:09,530
They're knockoffs.

66
00:05:11,923 --> 00:05:15,952
That belt and those shoes,

67
00:05:16,379 --> 00:05:19,172
all of it was fake, then?

68
00:05:19,331 --> 00:05:23,073
That guy, the knockoff guy, right?

69
00:05:23,964 --> 00:05:26,431
Yes, that's me.

70
00:05:26,531 --> 00:05:30,431
But they weren't knockoffs,
I should tell you that now.

71
00:05:30,831 --> 00:05:33,281
- They were real?
- Yes.

72
00:05:34,431 --> 00:05:36,531
- Hey, come inside first.
- Should I go out?

73
00:05:36,564 --> 00:05:40,031
Yes, go. What if Dad
says something rude to him?

74
00:05:42,197 --> 00:05:43,264
Me?

75
00:05:43,564 --> 00:05:46,031
Who else is standing here besides you?

76
00:05:47,031 --> 00:05:49,131
- Come in and we'll talk. Come on.
- Sir...

77
00:05:49,131 --> 00:05:51,597
I stopped by after a workout,
so I'm in sweats.

78
00:05:51,631 --> 00:05:53,264
I'll go home, change, and come right back.

79
00:05:53,331 --> 00:05:56,187
Am I here to talk to your sweats?

80
00:05:56,364 --> 00:06:00,235
Come in and we'll talk. Just come in.

81
00:06:01,931 --> 00:06:03,231
Come on in.

82
00:06:03,564 --> 00:06:07,131
Gyeol, I came straight from my workout
without washing up.

83
00:06:07,231 --> 00:06:10,664
I haven't washed my face and my hair
is from yesterday. Is that okay?

84
00:06:10,864 --> 00:06:15,364
It's fine. You're so handsome
nobody can tell.

85
00:06:17,257 --> 00:06:18,482
What are you waiting for?

86
00:06:18,864 --> 00:06:21,231
- I'm trying to come in.
- Hurry up. Get in here.

87
00:06:27,831 --> 00:06:30,267
Hey, get in here.

88
00:06:30,292 --> 00:06:31,801
Gyeol, you come in too.

89
00:06:31,877 --> 00:06:35,810
Hey, get in. Gyu Rim. Everyone gather.

90
00:06:36,564 --> 00:06:39,431
Hey, I peeked earlier.

91
00:06:39,531 --> 00:06:42,268
- Hello, Mu Jin.
- Welcome, Mu Jin.

92
00:06:42,339 --> 00:06:45,239
What? You all know each other?

93
00:06:45,264 --> 00:06:48,908
Yes, I'm going to go show U Ram
the rare Powerball card.

94
00:06:50,731 --> 00:06:55,407
So everyone knows everyone but me?

95
00:06:55,731 --> 00:06:56,931
I'm the only one left out?

96
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,491
Nobody left you out on purpose.

97
00:06:58,831 --> 00:07:01,531
You can't keep taking things
that way, Dad.

98
00:07:04,331 --> 00:07:07,764
Since you're seated, let me introduce
myself properly.

99
00:07:08,231 --> 00:07:11,134
Why would I hear you out? Who are you?

100
00:07:11,364 --> 00:07:14,764
Are you seeing my Gyu Rim again
or something?

101
00:07:18,764 --> 00:07:20,831
I care about your daughter very much.

102
00:07:20,931 --> 00:07:24,331
Gyu Rim hasn't accepted how I feel yet,
of course,

103
00:07:24,631 --> 00:07:28,231
which is why I'd like your help, sir.

104
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:32,431
Why would I help someone like you?
A broke knockoff...

105
00:07:32,531 --> 00:07:35,231
- daring to go after my daughter.
- Dad.

106
00:07:36,731 --> 00:07:39,631
I won't deny that I'm going after
your lovely daughter.

107
00:07:39,631 --> 00:07:42,664
But that watch, that belt, those shoes,

108
00:07:42,831 --> 00:07:45,131
they weren't knockoffs.
I'll say it again...

109
00:07:45,131 --> 00:07:47,231
He isn't broke, Dad.

110
00:07:47,331 --> 00:07:49,964
He's the head chef and owner
of the restaurant where I work.

111
00:07:50,631 --> 00:07:53,764
You own a restaurant?

112
00:07:53,831 --> 00:07:55,164
I co-own it with a friend.

113
00:07:55,864 --> 00:07:59,331
Co-owner? What, some hole in the wall?

114
00:07:59,331 --> 00:08:02,974
It's huge, Dad. Anyone in the know
has heard of that restaurant.

115
00:08:04,631 --> 00:08:07,278
All right.
What about a house? Do you own it?

116
00:08:08,531 --> 00:08:09,631
Dad.

117
00:08:10,531 --> 00:08:15,131
I don't own it. It's part deposit,
part monthly rent...

118
00:08:15,231 --> 00:08:17,964
What have you been doing
that you still don't own a house?

119
00:08:18,131 --> 00:08:20,531
Buying luxury watches, belts, and shoes?

120
00:08:20,664 --> 00:08:21,664
Dad.

121
00:08:21,988 --> 00:08:25,164
My savings account matures next year.
And I'll pull back my investments.

122
00:08:25,231 --> 00:08:30,364
Selling some stock and taking a loan,
I could afford a small apartment.

123
00:08:30,531 --> 00:08:31,831
Mu Jin, let's go.

124
00:08:32,631 --> 00:08:34,364
Nothing's broken upstairs, is it?

125
00:08:35,431 --> 00:08:38,631
Listening from up there,
you don't sound entirely normal.

126
00:08:39,131 --> 00:08:42,031
Han Gyu Rim isn't rich,
her skills aren't anything special,

127
00:08:42,131 --> 00:08:44,164
and she's a single mom with a son.

128
00:08:44,505 --> 00:08:48,250
Did you just get divorced?
How many kids do you have?

129
00:08:49,231 --> 00:08:54,431
I thought you'd have softened by now,
but you're as rotten as ever.

130
00:08:54,564 --> 00:08:57,031
What? You're talking down to me again.

131
00:08:57,057 --> 00:08:58,457
If it bothers you, drop the formality too.

132
00:08:59,817 --> 00:09:00,923
Unbelievable.

133
00:09:01,024 --> 00:09:03,117
Whatever.
Tangle up your own life, see if I care.

134
00:09:04,531 --> 00:09:06,542
Hey, Han Gyu Rim.
I told you not to trust people.

135
00:09:06,567 --> 00:09:08,176
Especially men, remember?

136
00:09:08,310 --> 00:09:09,877
Do you have to get burned to learn?

137
00:09:10,431 --> 00:09:12,864
Then go get burned good and hard.

138
00:09:13,231 --> 00:09:15,231
What a thing to say after all this time...

139
00:09:18,531 --> 00:09:21,164
That one must have put you through a lot.

140
00:09:22,364 --> 00:09:24,564
You have no idea how hard
and painful it's been...

141
00:09:25,764 --> 00:09:30,131
But have you been after my Gyu Rim
for eight straight years?

142
00:09:30,931 --> 00:09:36,006
Or did you take a break somewhere
and come back, like Gyu Yeong said?

143
00:09:36,031 --> 00:09:38,031
Personally, I never took a break.

144
00:09:38,431 --> 00:09:40,831
- Mu Jin, let's go. Come on.
- Why?

145
00:09:40,864 --> 00:09:42,431
I'm still talking.

146
00:09:42,431 --> 00:09:45,031
Next time I'll come dressed properly
and greet you the right way.

147
00:09:45,531 --> 00:09:49,264
Hey, sweats. I'm not finished
talking to you.

148
00:09:49,731 --> 00:09:51,631
Pathetic, honestly.

149
00:09:57,731 --> 00:10:00,164
Why answer every ridiculous thing he says?

150
00:10:01,531 --> 00:10:04,268
He's entitled to wonder. Any father would.

151
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:08,931
Still, I should have dressed up
to meet him.

152
00:10:09,564 --> 00:10:11,331
What if he's written me off again?

153
00:10:11,931 --> 00:10:13,542
Don't do this, Mu Jin.

154
00:10:14,662 --> 00:10:17,549
You and I can't happen.

155
00:10:18,570 --> 00:10:21,126
- We really can't.
- Why?

156
00:10:22,473 --> 00:10:24,731
Why not, and why can't we?

157
00:10:27,983 --> 00:10:30,188
- Do you really not know?
- I don't.

158
00:10:31,131 --> 00:10:32,131
I'm a single mom.

159
00:10:32,331 --> 00:10:33,931
That's solved if you marry me.

160
00:10:34,031 --> 00:10:35,198
Mu Jin.

161
00:10:35,531 --> 00:10:40,531
Even if I can't be a great father,
I could be a good one to Gyeol...

162
00:10:41,264 --> 00:10:46,231
No. Good father, great father,
handsome father, I can be all of them.

163
00:10:46,264 --> 00:10:49,231
Go ask anyone on the street.

164
00:10:49,631 --> 00:10:52,731
Whether a woman like me makes sense
for a man like you.

165
00:10:53,464 --> 00:10:55,219
You're the only one I have.

166
00:10:55,438 --> 00:10:57,431
If it's not you, I don't want anyone else.

167
00:10:57,464 --> 00:10:59,231
Why would I ask a stranger on the street?

168
00:11:01,164 --> 00:11:03,331
And why do you talk about
yourself so cruelly?

169
00:11:03,764 --> 00:11:07,631
Han Gyu Rim, you are precious
to me beyond words,

170
00:11:07,664 --> 00:11:11,031
so why do you define yourself
and put yourself down like that?

171
00:11:11,131 --> 00:11:13,731
Say that one more time and I'll sue you
for defamation...

172
00:11:20,784 --> 00:11:22,424
You're too pretty. I can't even sue you.

173
00:11:25,264 --> 00:11:29,364
Anyway, I didn't wash my face today...

174
00:11:29,596 --> 00:11:31,963
so I'm not looking my best,
and my hair is from yesterday.

175
00:11:32,381 --> 00:11:33,671
I can't stay long today.

176
00:11:33,831 --> 00:11:38,504
Let's meet again when I've cleaned up
a little. All right, Gyu Rim?

177
00:11:39,919 --> 00:11:41,064
Bye.

178
00:11:53,831 --> 00:11:55,204
Mu Jin is gone.

179
00:12:19,531 --> 00:12:22,408
Did Mu Jin go to Han Gyu Rim?

180
00:12:22,864 --> 00:12:24,964
Why do you care either way?

181
00:12:25,831 --> 00:12:30,414
Gyu Rim came first, before you.

182
00:12:31,564 --> 00:12:34,341
- Jeong Woo.
- For eight years, Mu Jin...

183
00:12:34,831 --> 00:12:37,431
never forgot Gyu Rim. Not for one moment.

184
00:12:38,164 --> 00:12:42,231
Did any other woman move him,
including you? Not for one second.

185
00:12:42,331 --> 00:12:44,631
- Jeong Woo.
- Kim Mu Jin has one heart.

186
00:12:45,831 --> 00:12:48,731
You didn't know? You knew.

187
00:12:49,831 --> 00:12:53,756
Out of guilt, out of obligation,
all you got from him was an empty shell,

188
00:12:54,564 --> 00:12:56,331
and you knew that better than anyone.

189
00:12:56,531 --> 00:12:58,931
Stop it. Who said I wanted to talk to you?

190
00:12:58,931 --> 00:13:03,431
Mu Jin did everything he could for you,

191
00:13:04,364 --> 00:13:06,764
and nobody could say
he didn't give it his all.

192
00:13:08,231 --> 00:13:11,731
If you're breaking up, break up cleanly.
Don't whine about it.

193
00:13:34,731 --> 00:13:36,464
That you aren't the Chairman's son,

194
00:13:36,731 --> 00:13:40,616
and that his wife gave birth
to Gyu Rim, Seo Hyeon knows all of it.

195
00:13:45,464 --> 00:13:50,864
That you and I both lied to her
and deceived her,

196
00:13:51,064 --> 00:13:53,031
she's going out of her mind over it.

197
00:14:02,631 --> 00:14:04,231
That's about as gentle as it gets.

198
00:14:04,577 --> 00:14:09,010
If I were Seo Hyeon,
one of us would be dead.

199
00:14:38,931 --> 00:14:40,299
Take it back.

200
00:14:42,764 --> 00:14:44,331
I'm not letting you go.

201
00:14:47,131 --> 00:14:49,190
I take back telling you
to go to Han Gyu Rim.

202
00:14:49,304 --> 00:14:51,230
You broke the rules first.

203
00:14:54,944 --> 00:14:56,646
So what if Kim Mu Jin is an empty shell.

204
00:14:57,793 --> 00:14:59,426
I'm not giving you to Han Gyu Rim.

205
00:15:06,564 --> 00:15:11,031
Why won't you say anything?
Say something, anything.

206
00:15:14,943 --> 00:15:16,231
I have nothing to say.

207
00:15:19,364 --> 00:15:20,431
Mu Jin.

208
00:15:23,931 --> 00:15:27,279
I have no excuse at all, not to you.

209
00:15:29,064 --> 00:15:30,607
Kim Mu Jin.

210
00:15:34,464 --> 00:15:35,631
I'm sorry, Seo Hyeon.

211
00:15:38,471 --> 00:15:41,786
I'll take whatever punishment I deserve
for hurting you.

212
00:16:15,331 --> 00:16:16,584
You've got insurance, right?

213
00:16:19,631 --> 00:16:21,664
Didn't that creep sign
you up for life insurance?

214
00:16:21,970 --> 00:16:23,459
What are you talking about now?

215
00:16:24,210 --> 00:16:27,470
Don't tell me you registered
the marriage already?

216
00:16:28,616 --> 00:16:29,798
Do I look like you?

217
00:16:34,605 --> 00:16:35,664
You saw the news, right?

218
00:16:35,964 --> 00:16:38,022
Registering the marriage
to collect on the policy,

219
00:16:38,047 --> 00:16:40,116
then staging an accident
and killing the spouse.

220
00:16:42,331 --> 00:16:44,898
Then why see a man you met
eight years ago again?

221
00:16:44,931 --> 00:16:47,131
You were broke then, and you're broke now,

222
00:16:47,164 --> 00:16:48,764
and now you've got
a kid dragging you down.

223
00:16:48,831 --> 00:16:50,631
How many policies do you have?

224
00:16:51,270 --> 00:16:53,476
Should I just push you off right here?

225
00:16:54,731 --> 00:16:56,141
Did you run some kind of scam?

226
00:16:56,331 --> 00:16:58,190
"Our mother is marrying into money."

227
00:16:58,231 --> 00:17:01,331
"If my stepfather dies,
half of it is hers, which makes me..."

228
00:17:01,631 --> 00:17:03,106
"basically an heiress."

229
00:17:03,131 --> 00:17:06,764
Stuffing your head with that
is what makes you a lowlife.

230
00:17:06,831 --> 00:17:09,031
- What? A lowlife?
- Yes.

231
00:17:09,431 --> 00:17:12,031
A total lowlife
with zero conscience or shame.

232
00:17:12,064 --> 00:17:13,064
Hey!

233
00:17:15,931 --> 00:17:17,731
You're the one who should
call off that wedding.

234
00:17:17,864 --> 00:17:22,764
Even now, beg for forgiveness,
say you're sorry for lying, and walk away.

235
00:17:23,131 --> 00:17:24,664
You're really going all the way...

236
00:17:25,064 --> 00:17:28,464
If you can't do it, I'll kneel
and beg for you.

237
00:17:29,231 --> 00:17:32,238
Let's do that, Gyu Yeong.
Before it's too late, please...

238
00:17:32,431 --> 00:17:36,448
It's my life. You said cut ties,
so what business is it of yours?

239
00:17:36,564 --> 00:17:39,931
You know what? If I could drain
the Han blood out of my body,

240
00:17:40,064 --> 00:17:42,164
I'd drain every drop of it. You hear me?

241
00:17:48,231 --> 00:17:50,731
Forget the highway I worked hard to pave,

242
00:17:51,431 --> 00:17:53,931
and worry about your own
dirt road going nowhere.

243
00:17:54,564 --> 00:17:58,164
Carry a silver spoon in case
someone poisons your food.

244
00:18:34,946 --> 00:18:36,964
He said the password was absurdly easy.

245
00:18:37,664 --> 00:18:40,264
Don't tell me it's one, two, three, four,
five, six?

246
00:18:41,631 --> 00:18:43,931
It can't be five, six, seven, eight,
nine, zero, can it?

247
00:18:45,531 --> 00:18:46,931
You have got to be kidding me.

248
00:18:52,504 --> 00:18:56,637
His name was Son Ji Yeol.

249
00:18:58,331 --> 00:19:01,786
Here it is. 010...

250
00:19:02,531 --> 00:19:07,442
4555 1717.

251
00:19:12,364 --> 00:19:13,431
What are you doing?

252
00:19:14,831 --> 00:19:17,731
You scared me. You don't even knock?

253
00:19:18,931 --> 00:19:22,525
- It's my room. Why would I knock?
- Right.

254
00:19:24,406 --> 00:19:25,531
What were you doing?

255
00:19:26,231 --> 00:19:27,964
You're too young to know.

256
00:19:28,531 --> 00:19:31,164
What is it? What are you up to now?

257
00:19:31,931 --> 00:19:33,231
You looked at Gyu O's phone, didn't you?

258
00:19:35,231 --> 00:19:36,664
Let go.

259
00:19:41,431 --> 00:19:42,631
Hey, twins.

260
00:19:44,997 --> 00:19:46,564
If you're going to fight, take it outside.

261
00:19:47,531 --> 00:19:51,297
I was heading out anyway. Sorry.

262
00:19:51,630 --> 00:19:52,930
Sleep well, Gyu O.

263
00:20:01,731 --> 00:20:02,831
Let me see that eye.

264
00:20:02,964 --> 00:20:04,928
It's fine. All healed.

265
00:20:05,031 --> 00:20:07,031
I want to see how ugly it got.

266
00:20:10,460 --> 00:20:12,631
How did you work
as an escort looking like that?

267
00:20:13,131 --> 00:20:14,131
What did you say?

268
00:20:14,131 --> 00:20:16,264
Were all your women nearsighted
or just out of their minds?

269
00:20:17,964 --> 00:20:21,031
What time is it? Don't you have school?

270
00:20:39,903 --> 00:20:42,646
- Where are you?
- Home.

271
00:20:44,264 --> 00:20:45,531
Turn the camera around.

272
00:20:56,031 --> 00:20:57,331
Han Gyu Seo?

273
00:20:59,731 --> 00:21:03,164
You must be Gyu O's brother. Hello.

274
00:21:04,964 --> 00:21:06,631
Yes, hello.

275
00:21:07,131 --> 00:21:09,707
I'm Kwon Hui Na, Han Gyu O's girlfriend.

276
00:21:12,464 --> 00:21:13,464
I see.

277
00:21:16,264 --> 00:21:18,442
Why the sudden video call?

278
00:21:19,524 --> 00:21:23,242
- I wanted to see your face too.
- What?

279
00:21:23,631 --> 00:21:25,331
Can you put your brother back on?

280
00:21:33,231 --> 00:21:37,268
I'll memorize it right away.
Could I get your number, Gyu Seo?

281
00:21:39,031 --> 00:21:40,626
Sure, mine is 010...

282
00:21:41,931 --> 00:21:44,064
What do you want with Gyu Seo's number?

283
00:21:44,164 --> 00:21:47,864
So I can ask him to watch
what you get up to when I'm not around.

284
00:21:48,131 --> 00:21:49,131
What?

285
00:21:49,331 --> 00:21:53,953
Mine is 010 0213 4187.

286
00:21:54,064 --> 00:21:55,179
Did you memorize it?

287
00:21:59,164 --> 00:22:02,545
Gyu Seo has to get to school. Talk later.

288
00:22:06,531 --> 00:22:09,088
- I asked if you have school.
- I'm going.

289
00:22:49,064 --> 00:22:50,166
Yes, this is Han Gyu Seo.

290
00:22:50,264 --> 00:22:52,664
It's Kwon Hui Na, from the video call.

291
00:22:53,531 --> 00:22:54,531
Yes.

292
00:22:56,064 --> 00:22:57,957
Let's be good to each other from now on.

293
00:22:59,131 --> 00:23:02,236
You'll see when we meet,
but I'm a teacher,

294
00:23:02,563 --> 00:23:04,536
and I'm a really good person.

295
00:23:05,031 --> 00:23:06,731
How long have you been seeing him?

296
00:23:07,231 --> 00:23:08,431
Day one was yesterday.

297
00:23:09,164 --> 00:23:11,848
How much do you know about him?

298
00:23:13,831 --> 00:23:15,728
How much am I supposed to know?

299
00:23:18,831 --> 00:23:20,699
I'm not interested in the before.

300
00:23:21,264 --> 00:23:24,831
What he did before he met me,
what women he saw,

301
00:23:25,231 --> 00:23:27,431
what job he had, why would I care?

302
00:23:28,531 --> 00:23:32,405
I only need to know Han Gyu O
from today on.

303
00:23:32,764 --> 00:23:36,431
What shampoo he uses, what food he likes,

304
00:23:36,731 --> 00:23:40,931
whether he snores,
what size shoe he wears.

305
00:23:41,431 --> 00:23:45,099
A field study of Han Gyu O.
Would you help me with that?

306
00:23:46,431 --> 00:23:47,431
Of course.

307
00:23:50,051 --> 00:23:53,345
Then could I ask you for one thing too?

308
00:23:55,231 --> 00:23:56,264
Of course.

309
00:23:57,681 --> 00:23:59,501
Whatever kind of person my brother is,

310
00:24:00,826 --> 00:24:05,169
even if he disappoints you,
please don't throw him away.

311
00:24:06,793 --> 00:24:08,980
You said you're a really good person.

312
00:24:09,240 --> 00:24:11,040
You're a teacher and an educator,

313
00:24:11,388 --> 00:24:13,674
so think of it
as teaching one failing student.

314
00:24:15,274 --> 00:24:17,354
All right. I'll never throw him away.

315
00:24:18,094 --> 00:24:19,888
If he tries to fly off and leave me,

316
00:24:19,924 --> 00:24:24,153
I'll snap his legs to keep him beside me,
so don't you worry.

317
00:24:30,502 --> 00:24:32,108
(Su Nam)

318
00:24:42,773 --> 00:24:44,847
(Su Nam)

319
00:24:48,021 --> 00:24:51,187
Gyu O, Why are you calling this early?

320
00:24:52,172 --> 00:24:55,248
Did something happen to your sister?

321
00:24:56,580 --> 00:24:58,128
You know Kwon Hui Na, right?

322
00:24:59,114 --> 00:25:01,120
Could I get her parents' number?

323
00:25:02,301 --> 00:25:05,094
What do you want with Hui Na's parents?

324
00:25:06,694 --> 00:25:08,832
Did something happen to Hui Na?

325
00:25:10,781 --> 00:25:12,654
There's this lowlife.

326
00:25:13,665 --> 00:25:16,854
He doesn't know his place and he likes
Kwon Hui Na far too much.

327
00:25:18,394 --> 00:25:21,167
And Hui Na's too soft to know
how cruel the world is.

328
00:25:23,314 --> 00:25:27,056
Before it gets out of hand,
her parents need to come,

329
00:25:28,162 --> 00:25:30,093
and pry that piece of trash off her.

330
00:25:30,727 --> 00:25:33,907
What kind of nonsense is that?

331
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:37,495
Who is this rotten lowlife?

332
00:25:38,162 --> 00:25:39,674
No need to go to her parents.

333
00:25:39,734 --> 00:25:41,653
I'm as good as Hui Na's parent,

334
00:25:41,861 --> 00:25:43,961
so you tell me who he is.

335
00:25:44,193 --> 00:25:47,453
I'll go straight over
and crack his skull open.

336
00:25:47,973 --> 00:25:49,528
Who is he?

337
00:25:49,656 --> 00:25:51,820
Give me his name and address, now.

338
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:57,748
I'm sorry.

339
00:25:59,452 --> 00:26:00,813
I'll tell you another time.

340
00:26:15,840 --> 00:26:18,514
Hey, Gyu O, you rotten boy!

341
00:26:20,133 --> 00:26:21,178
- Honestly...
- What?

342
00:26:22,167 --> 00:26:25,300
Did his sisters give him lessons...

343
00:26:25,325 --> 00:26:27,334
in driving people out of their minds?

344
00:26:27,441 --> 00:26:29,500
- What?
- Who hangs up mid-call?

345
00:26:30,007 --> 00:26:31,600
What about Gyu O? What happened?

346
00:26:32,493 --> 00:26:36,209
Some damn fool is crazy about Hui Na,

347
00:26:36,317 --> 00:26:39,140
and her parents need
to come put a stop to it.

348
00:26:39,854 --> 00:26:42,447
What? Who's this damn fool?

349
00:26:42,641 --> 00:26:43,816
Someone Gyu O knows?

350
00:26:44,267 --> 00:26:47,386
No. You stay out of it.

351
00:26:48,156 --> 00:26:50,678
Throw one more punch
over someone else's business,

352
00:26:50,703 --> 00:26:52,194
and what did I say I'd do?

353
00:26:52,994 --> 00:26:55,852
That you'd wrap me up in your skirt,

354
00:26:56,160 --> 00:26:57,880
and dive into the Han River with me.

355
00:26:57,881 --> 00:26:59,195
That's right.

356
00:26:59,392 --> 00:27:02,830
That day you die and I go down with you.

357
00:27:03,098 --> 00:27:04,338
- Understood?
- Understood.

358
00:27:06,327 --> 00:27:10,654
But how does Gyu O know Hui Na so well?

359
00:27:11,107 --> 00:27:13,933
Did they get in touch and meet somehow?

360
00:27:15,566 --> 00:27:18,707
Why are you eavesdropping on me?

361
00:27:18,732 --> 00:27:20,200
Are we strangers?

362
00:27:22,671 --> 00:27:26,332
And we're having sashimi for lunch,
so keep breakfast light.

363
00:27:26,827 --> 00:27:27,830
- Sashimi?
- Yes.

364
00:27:27,958 --> 00:27:29,367
Sashimi out of nowhere?

365
00:27:29,521 --> 00:27:33,426
You won the lottery and thought you'd
wipe your mouth and walk away?

366
00:27:35,453 --> 00:27:38,818
You'd pick bean sprouts out of a beggar's
backside. You sneaky brat!

367
00:27:42,635 --> 00:27:44,415
(Conger Eel in Season)

368
00:27:49,492 --> 00:27:54,020
What? Are those flowers for me?

369
00:27:55,069 --> 00:27:58,694
Who else would I give them to,
this old guy?

370
00:27:59,561 --> 00:28:02,081
Congratulations on your lottery win...

371
00:28:03,589 --> 00:28:07,234
Anyone listening would think I won
millions and turned my life around.

372
00:28:09,820 --> 00:28:14,019
I won a thousand dollars. Just a thousand.

373
00:28:14,768 --> 00:28:18,567
If a thief breaks in thinking I'm rich,
are you taking responsibility?

374
00:28:20,847 --> 00:28:23,699
Either way, the ticket I bought you won,

375
00:28:23,813 --> 00:28:26,390
so my family can stop fearing eviction,

376
00:28:26,415 --> 00:28:28,346
and just live in peace, right?

377
00:28:28,621 --> 00:28:29,621
Of course.

378
00:28:29,835 --> 00:28:33,433
You can stay as long as you like,
for the rest of your life.

379
00:28:34,041 --> 00:28:35,562
Is that house yours to give?

380
00:28:36,467 --> 00:28:38,807
Instead of blaming someone else's mouth,

381
00:28:38,901 --> 00:28:41,494
I should start with my own son's.

382
00:28:42,974 --> 00:28:45,607
What do I do with this traitor?

383
00:28:45,632 --> 00:28:49,134
Let's not do this. Sit down,
have some sashimi,

384
00:28:49,159 --> 00:28:50,734
- and talk it over.
- Yes.

385
00:28:50,974 --> 00:28:54,034
So, ma'am, should we go farmed? Or...

386
00:28:54,094 --> 00:28:56,294
You'd prefer wild-caught,
right? Wild-caught.

387
00:28:56,561 --> 00:28:59,658
- Wild-caught it is.
- Wild-caught. Let's go.

388
00:29:01,072 --> 00:29:02,645
Sit down.

389
00:29:05,341 --> 00:29:07,958
Rich and tasty.

390
00:29:10,607 --> 00:29:14,520
Next time I'll buy you wild-caught.
Same hour.

391
00:29:15,654 --> 00:29:17,494
You don't earn a cent,

392
00:29:17,814 --> 00:29:21,585
yet you're buying something that expensive
for this useless old man?

393
00:29:22,581 --> 00:29:25,342
A useless old man?

394
00:29:25,893 --> 00:29:28,372
And who bought you the winning ticket?

395
00:29:29,514 --> 00:29:31,210
If you keep nagging me like this,

396
00:29:31,864 --> 00:29:33,807
the swallow that brought
the seed will fly off again.

397
00:29:33,909 --> 00:29:37,267
Fly away. It won't bother me one bit.

398
00:29:38,233 --> 00:29:41,057
Why are you doing
this at a nice lunch, Mom?

399
00:29:42,269 --> 00:29:47,076
Anyway, let's clear away all the bad blood
with this,

400
00:29:47,212 --> 00:29:49,394
and you two shake hands.

401
00:29:49,515 --> 00:29:51,427
Let's make peace. Shake.

402
00:29:51,634 --> 00:29:52,874
Shake.

403
00:29:56,256 --> 00:30:00,731
Why does it feel like I'm the only one
losing out here,

404
00:30:01,539 --> 00:30:04,174
over a measly thousand dollars?

405
00:30:05,674 --> 00:30:07,082
Help me out, ma'am.

406
00:30:07,502 --> 00:30:10,562
I really don't want
to be thrown out like this.

407
00:30:12,453 --> 00:30:14,306
Gyu Rim's mother came by a while ago,

408
00:30:14,607 --> 00:30:17,063
saying she'd find me a house
in the country,

409
00:30:17,065 --> 00:30:19,306
and telling me to take the kids
and leave Seoul,

410
00:30:19,521 --> 00:30:21,981
and it crushed me. I couldn't believe it.

411
00:30:23,013 --> 00:30:25,241
Really? Gyu Rim's mother showed up?

412
00:30:25,601 --> 00:30:26,727
Seriously?

413
00:30:27,316 --> 00:30:31,317
She shows up and tells you to leave Seoul
with all the kids?

414
00:30:31,437 --> 00:30:34,234
That woman remarried into money.

415
00:30:34,894 --> 00:30:37,233
I guess she's afraid we'll cling to her.

416
00:30:37,341 --> 00:30:42,072
Should I go ask that rich husband
to buy me a house?

417
00:30:42,288 --> 00:30:44,974
That two-story mansion
in Pyeongchang Dong.

418
00:30:45,561 --> 00:30:47,641
Don't talk nonsense.

419
00:30:48,141 --> 00:30:50,752
- Have you no pride as a man?
- No pride here.

420
00:30:51,786 --> 00:30:53,040
Does pride put food on the table?

421
00:30:54,634 --> 00:30:55,646
If I hadn't given her that divorce,

422
00:30:55,757 --> 00:30:58,067
how would he have married a woman
that fine?

423
00:30:58,303 --> 00:30:59,447
Look at Gyu Rim's mother.

424
00:30:59,571 --> 00:31:02,207
Kind? Smart? Good at running a home?

425
00:31:07,654 --> 00:31:10,451
Should I ask for a shop
instead of a house?

426
00:31:13,721 --> 00:31:15,681
Ma'am, what's a shop going for these days?

427
00:32:00,482 --> 00:32:01,942
(Daughter)

428
00:32:08,006 --> 00:32:10,855
The call cannot be connected
and will go to voicemail.

429
00:32:10,880 --> 00:32:13,219
Charges apply after the beep.

430
00:32:28,460 --> 00:32:32,300
Seo Hyeon. I packed you a lunchbox.

431
00:32:33,454 --> 00:32:35,449
I'm at the coffee shop near your office.

432
00:32:35,762 --> 00:32:39,174
Could you step out and pick it up?

433
00:32:45,359 --> 00:32:48,123
- Who is it?
- No one.

434
00:32:49,527 --> 00:32:50,783
Your father is coming.

435
00:32:51,073 --> 00:32:52,859
I told him you were having lunch here.

436
00:32:52,987 --> 00:32:54,891
Why do things nobody asked you to?

437
00:33:01,564 --> 00:33:03,174
Hey, I heard this place is good.

438
00:33:06,782 --> 00:33:07,935
Seo Hyeon.

439
00:33:09,507 --> 00:33:12,968
I haven't eaten all day.
Let's eat together.

440
00:33:13,587 --> 00:33:15,587
Doesn't Ko Yun Hui cook for you?

441
00:33:18,379 --> 00:33:19,579
Sit.

442
00:33:27,380 --> 00:33:30,027
(Daughter)

443
00:33:42,247 --> 00:33:43,247
It's good.

444
00:33:43,675 --> 00:33:45,458
Why aren't you eating? Eat.

445
00:33:48,354 --> 00:33:51,568
I'll give you two some privacy
so you can talk.

446
00:33:52,072 --> 00:33:53,253
No need to leave.

447
00:33:53,754 --> 00:33:55,654
There's nothing here you can't hear.

448
00:33:56,991 --> 00:34:00,738
Seo Hyeon's state of mind
is like dry kindling set on fire,

449
00:34:01,181 --> 00:34:04,676
so I'll stay a moment to help put it out.

450
00:34:05,763 --> 00:34:06,936
All right.

451
00:34:10,494 --> 00:34:11,915
It was all my fault.

452
00:34:13,074 --> 00:34:16,158
I didn't think it through,

453
00:34:17,740 --> 00:34:19,575
and as a father and as a grown man,

454
00:34:19,576 --> 00:34:22,334
I'm too ashamed to lift my head.

455
00:34:23,573 --> 00:34:25,873
I'm truly sorry, Seo Hyeon.

456
00:34:28,346 --> 00:34:29,789
Let's talk about this among ourselves,

457
00:34:30,018 --> 00:34:31,975
- and eat for now.
- Yes.

458
00:34:33,194 --> 00:34:35,390
If you're sorry, divorce her. Ko Yun Hui.

459
00:34:38,708 --> 00:34:40,446
Your mother did nothing wrong.

460
00:34:40,761 --> 00:34:41,934
How did she do nothing wrong?

461
00:34:42,787 --> 00:34:44,753
Giving birth to someone
like Han Gyu Rim is wrong enough.

462
00:34:45,360 --> 00:34:46,360
Seo Hyeon.

463
00:34:46,881 --> 00:34:48,714
If that girl had never existed,

464
00:34:48,888 --> 00:34:50,693
if Ko Yun Hui weren't her mother,

465
00:34:50,695 --> 00:34:52,780
none of this would have landed on me.

466
00:34:55,408 --> 00:34:58,007
I wish someone
like Han Gyu Rim would vanish.

467
00:35:02,480 --> 00:35:04,694
Is this all you amount to?

468
00:35:09,388 --> 00:35:11,118
I think I raised you wrong.

469
00:35:12,811 --> 00:35:13,907
Dad.

470
00:35:14,520 --> 00:35:15,540
Your mother...

471
00:35:17,068 --> 00:35:20,101
No, fine. Ko Yun Hui...

472
00:35:20,685 --> 00:35:24,004
turned away from the children she bore
to raise you well,

473
00:35:25,038 --> 00:35:27,420
and never had another child with me.

474
00:35:27,780 --> 00:35:30,040
I don't think that was right of her.

475
00:35:31,021 --> 00:35:33,033
Still, you of all people
can't do that to her,

476
00:35:34,131 --> 00:35:36,359
or to that girl Han Gyu Rim.

477
00:35:36,934 --> 00:35:38,640
Are you taking Han Gyu Rim's side?

478
00:35:38,641 --> 00:35:40,631
I'm not taking sides.
I'm talking about you.

479
00:35:42,674 --> 00:35:44,214
Is what you're doing love?

480
00:35:46,020 --> 00:35:47,660
Then don't. Don't do it at all.

481
00:35:48,533 --> 00:35:51,152
I don't want you breaking yourself
and turning into a monster,

482
00:35:51,177 --> 00:35:52,583
so don't love like that.

483
00:35:52,631 --> 00:35:53,761
Dad.

484
00:35:56,230 --> 00:35:57,307
Mu Jin?

485
00:35:57,741 --> 00:35:58,781
Right...

486
00:36:00,776 --> 00:36:02,028
The way I see it now,

487
00:36:02,576 --> 00:36:06,428
you don't deserve to love Mu Jin
or be loved by him.

488
00:36:08,566 --> 00:36:10,194
I'm sorry for saying something like that.

489
00:36:10,581 --> 00:36:11,974
Mu Jin dodged that well.

490
00:36:12,568 --> 00:36:14,101
At least there's that.

491
00:37:04,420 --> 00:37:05,420
Honey.

492
00:37:05,868 --> 00:37:08,473
If there's anyone you should be sorry to,

493
00:37:09,282 --> 00:37:12,751
it's the children you bore,
especially Gyu Rim.

494
00:37:13,307 --> 00:37:14,920
Only Gyu Rim.

495
00:37:46,567 --> 00:37:49,373
- Hello.
- Hello.

496
00:37:50,834 --> 00:37:52,527
You came by before, didn't you?

497
00:37:53,888 --> 00:37:55,361
Yes.

498
00:37:55,554 --> 00:37:58,792
We have a lot of good side dishes today.
Try some before you go.

499
00:37:59,133 --> 00:38:02,086
No. I'm not here for side dishes.

500
00:38:03,808 --> 00:38:07,647
Have you eaten, by any chance?

501
00:38:09,362 --> 00:38:11,827
Yes. I had lunch.

502
00:38:13,349 --> 00:38:14,713
Of course.

503
00:38:15,614 --> 00:38:17,643
Lunchtime was a while ago.

504
00:38:19,350 --> 00:38:21,194
Have you had dinner?

505
00:38:22,048 --> 00:38:25,853
I was going to eat at home later.

506
00:38:27,709 --> 00:38:29,173
Then...

507
00:38:31,060 --> 00:38:33,215
would you like this for dinner?

508
00:38:36,054 --> 00:38:38,300
It's a lunchbox I made myself,

509
00:38:38,985 --> 00:38:41,506
and I made it really well.

510
00:38:43,214 --> 00:38:45,634
You're giving this to me?

511
00:38:47,481 --> 00:38:50,460
If it makes you uncomfortable,
don't eat it.

512
00:38:50,494 --> 00:38:51,867
Not at all. I'll take it.

513
00:38:52,006 --> 00:38:56,039
You said you made it well,
so I'm grateful. I'll take it.

514
00:39:00,660 --> 00:39:02,713
Thank you. I'll enjoy it.

515
00:39:38,213 --> 00:39:40,768
A grown man, old as he is,

516
00:39:40,770 --> 00:39:43,667
how can he be that childish?

517
00:39:44,761 --> 00:39:46,934
Being childish is a talent too.

518
00:39:48,759 --> 00:39:52,257
Someone walks in
and you don't even notice?

519
00:39:53,301 --> 00:39:54,640
Welcome, Su Nam.

520
00:39:55,654 --> 00:39:58,729
Young as you are, where's your head at?

521
00:40:01,763 --> 00:40:03,786
What in the world is all this?

522
00:40:04,733 --> 00:40:08,756
Someone gave it to me a moment ago.

523
00:40:10,214 --> 00:40:11,487
Someone who?

524
00:40:17,137 --> 00:40:21,271
What has you so completely out of it?

525
00:40:24,086 --> 00:40:25,361
Is something wrong?

526
00:40:26,306 --> 00:40:27,549
This lunchbox...

527
00:40:29,295 --> 00:40:32,217
looks like one I've seen before.

528
00:40:33,107 --> 00:40:34,107
What?

529
00:40:35,516 --> 00:40:36,721
This lunchbox...

530
00:40:39,234 --> 00:40:44,718
looks exactly
like the ones my mother packed me.

531
00:40:46,245 --> 00:40:47,863
Don't lie to me.

532
00:40:47,911 --> 00:40:50,420
You ate lunches this fancy?

533
00:40:52,508 --> 00:40:55,640
You said you grew up rich, didn't you?

534
00:40:57,711 --> 00:41:01,258
It's good!

535
00:41:05,860 --> 00:41:09,556
This abalone tastes like citron.

536
00:41:15,616 --> 00:41:20,158
When my mother braised abalone,

537
00:41:22,119 --> 00:41:23,774
she put in citron syrup.

538
00:41:28,554 --> 00:41:31,826
That woman who gave you this lunchbox,

539
00:41:32,385 --> 00:41:36,103
was she wearing dark sunglasses?
Like a spy?

540
00:41:38,727 --> 00:41:42,447
I knew it. They said your mother
went to see your father too.

541
00:41:43,052 --> 00:41:46,738
That woman is your mother.

542
00:41:46,874 --> 00:41:51,793
She came before and asked
if you were Han Gyu Rim.

543
00:41:52,597 --> 00:41:57,139
But why leave the lunchbox and go
without saying who she was?

544
00:41:58,581 --> 00:42:01,900
If she just left, she can't be far.

545
00:42:21,334 --> 00:42:22,860
Got you! You spy lady.

546
00:42:23,356 --> 00:42:24,974
You're Han Gyu Rim's mother, aren't you?

547
00:42:26,080 --> 00:42:28,098
You are. Han Gyu Rim's mother.

548
00:42:28,123 --> 00:42:29,828
You have the wrong person.

549
00:42:30,301 --> 00:42:32,320
Take off those dark glasses.

550
00:42:32,834 --> 00:42:35,651
Let me get a look at that face,

551
00:42:35,724 --> 00:42:37,624
and see how expensive and grand it is.

552
00:42:37,746 --> 00:42:39,582
Coming to your child
after all these years,

553
00:42:39,623 --> 00:42:42,934
and walking off without a word.
Let me see that fine face!

554
00:42:42,959 --> 00:42:44,340
This old woman, honestly!

555
00:42:44,381 --> 00:42:46,200
I told you, you have the wrong person.

556
00:42:47,014 --> 00:42:51,247
Afraid they'd cling to you,
like Gyu Rim's father said?

557
00:42:54,074 --> 00:42:56,687
I heard you remarried a rich chairman.

558
00:42:56,827 --> 00:43:00,394
Scared the kids will ask you for money?

559
00:43:00,414 --> 00:43:02,034
This old woman, honestly.

560
00:43:02,454 --> 00:43:05,087
Stop saying strange things
and see a doctor if you're sick.

561
00:43:05,220 --> 00:43:09,068
Keep blocking my way like this
and I'll call the police.

562
00:43:13,833 --> 00:43:16,448
Truly heartless and cold.

563
00:43:17,427 --> 00:43:19,347
Standing in front of the child you bore,

564
00:43:19,349 --> 00:43:22,675
how can you not say you're her mother?

565
00:43:23,061 --> 00:43:24,991
They say blood is thicker than water,

566
00:43:24,993 --> 00:43:27,621
but is yours made of ice water?

567
00:43:29,861 --> 00:43:31,754
What a ruthless woman.

568
00:44:29,461 --> 00:44:30,641
Are you all right?

569
00:44:38,462 --> 00:44:42,076
You're that student from last time, right?

570
00:44:42,640 --> 00:44:45,202
Yes. You're okay?

571
00:44:46,027 --> 00:44:47,610
I'm fine.

572
00:44:50,659 --> 00:44:53,224
I was lost in thought...

573
00:44:55,267 --> 00:44:58,237
If it weren't for you,
that could have been bad.

574
00:44:59,427 --> 00:45:01,534
Thank you, twice now.

575
00:45:05,054 --> 00:45:06,686
You're Han Gyu Rim's mother, aren't you?

576
00:45:37,200 --> 00:45:40,394
What kind of ruthless woman is that?

577
00:45:40,820 --> 00:45:44,596
Looking closely, she's the spitting image
of your mother.

578
00:45:45,020 --> 00:45:47,154
Insisting it wasn't her to the end,

579
00:45:47,853 --> 00:45:50,593
she's a cold-blooded one, that woman.

580
00:45:52,287 --> 00:45:53,861
Mom!

581
00:45:54,614 --> 00:45:56,366
She's gone. Your mother.

582
00:45:58,587 --> 00:45:59,740
Mom!

583
00:45:59,874 --> 00:46:01,827
She can't hear you.

584
00:46:01,954 --> 00:46:03,994
You should have called out
when you had her!

585
00:46:04,894 --> 00:46:06,667
Mom!

586
00:46:09,480 --> 00:46:13,711
That's right.
How long have you wanted to call her that?

587
00:46:14,547 --> 00:46:18,058
She might hear your voice and come back,

588
00:46:18,083 --> 00:46:19,961
so call out louder.

589
00:46:23,353 --> 00:46:30,058
Mom!

590
00:46:31,351 --> 00:46:33,271
Mom.

591
00:46:40,254 --> 00:46:42,105
- What brings you here at this hour?
- Hey.

592
00:46:42,560 --> 00:46:44,701
- Hello, sir.
- Hello.

593
00:46:45,277 --> 00:46:47,414
I heard you were here,
so I came to say hello.

594
00:46:47,507 --> 00:46:49,200
- Have you been well?
- Of course.

595
00:46:50,787 --> 00:46:52,767
I'll leave you two to talk.

596
00:46:52,792 --> 00:46:55,282
- Tell Secretary Kim I won't need the tea.
- Yes.

597
00:47:00,733 --> 00:47:03,513
From your face, this isn't good news.

598
00:47:04,654 --> 00:47:08,454
Hey, have you ever met Han Gyu Rim?

599
00:47:09,486 --> 00:47:11,959
Why is her name coming out of your mouth?

600
00:47:12,150 --> 00:47:17,031
It's just that, even after all this time,

601
00:47:17,062 --> 00:47:20,453
he can't forget her. He still cares...

602
00:47:20,757 --> 00:47:23,333
Have you thought about letting them be?

603
00:47:25,847 --> 00:47:28,719
Is Mu Jin holding something over you?
Is he blackmailing you?

604
00:47:29,039 --> 00:47:31,226
What kind of nonsense is that?

605
00:47:31,417 --> 00:47:33,594
Don't you know who Han Gyu Rim is?

606
00:47:33,627 --> 00:47:35,264
I know. Of course I do.

607
00:47:35,728 --> 00:47:37,734
Right, a girl who never went
to college, as you say.

608
00:47:38,120 --> 00:47:43,620
But she missed college because
she was the breadwinner, earning money,

609
00:47:43,720 --> 00:47:45,426
looking after her siblings.
That's all it was.

610
00:47:45,451 --> 00:47:48,175
And that also makes her selfless,

611
00:47:48,245 --> 00:47:51,860
thoughtful, and full of responsibility,
doesn't it?

612
00:47:51,885 --> 00:47:54,612
- Hey!
- You scared me.

613
00:47:55,974 --> 00:47:57,407
You, honestly.

614
00:47:57,427 --> 00:47:59,457
I've long known
you aren't in your right mind,

615
00:47:59,459 --> 00:48:01,687
but a woman makes you lose all sense.

616
00:48:01,715 --> 00:48:04,219
It wasn't enough to ruin your own life,

617
00:48:04,220 --> 00:48:06,618
so you're ruining my precious son?

618
00:48:06,647 --> 00:48:07,754
Calm down.

619
00:48:07,779 --> 00:48:12,420
If Seo Hyeon finds out, you two
are enemies as father and daughter.

620
00:48:12,441 --> 00:48:15,998
I'm not talking about me and Seo Hyeon.
I'm talking about your son.

621
00:48:16,201 --> 00:48:19,007
That's what makes Mu Jin happy.

622
00:48:19,221 --> 00:48:20,634
Honestly, Seo Hyeon and Mu Jin?

623
00:48:20,659 --> 00:48:21,834
I really don't know.

624
00:48:21,927 --> 00:48:24,740
I think those two would be miserable.

625
00:48:24,765 --> 00:48:28,413
This is driving me crazy. Hey!

626
00:48:29,007 --> 00:48:32,645
You're a man who dotes on his daughter,

627
00:48:32,692 --> 00:48:34,760
so how did you end up like this?

628
00:48:35,146 --> 00:48:40,346
Hey, Ko Yun Hui took care of your mother
for ten years,

629
00:48:40,348 --> 00:48:42,947
- so now you're drowning in gratitude?
- Hey.

630
00:48:43,012 --> 00:48:47,379
Mu Jin is a fine
and admirable young man, your son.

631
00:48:47,541 --> 00:48:48,727
Enough that I envy you.

632
00:48:48,820 --> 00:48:54,140
But right now Gyu Rim is all Mu Jin has.

633
00:48:54,454 --> 00:48:55,751
You know that too, don't you?

634
00:48:56,013 --> 00:48:58,459
How Mu Jin has spent the last eight years.

635
00:48:58,712 --> 00:49:02,706
He gave up everything for Gyu Rim
and has lived that way ever since.

636
00:49:02,881 --> 00:49:06,352
Honestly, I don't know what Mu Jin feels
when he's with Seo Hyeon.

637
00:49:06,420 --> 00:49:09,188
Maybe it's out of duty, I don't know,

638
00:49:09,215 --> 00:49:13,252
but either way, Gyu Rim
is all Mu Jin has now.

639
00:49:13,660 --> 00:49:15,121
You, honestly.

640
00:49:15,146 --> 00:49:17,869
Hey, you'll be punished for trying
to tear two people like that apart.

641
00:49:17,894 --> 00:49:19,627
Jang Hun Tae!

642
00:49:19,719 --> 00:49:21,426
Anyway, you can't stop him.

643
00:49:21,640 --> 00:49:23,614
You'll never stop Mu Jin,

644
00:49:23,687 --> 00:49:26,860
so since you can't, just accept it.

645
00:49:26,960 --> 00:49:29,460
Stop hurting each other and accept it.

646
00:49:29,526 --> 00:49:31,240
Delete my number as of today.

647
00:49:31,324 --> 00:49:35,792
If you're going to spout this nonsense,
don't call me. Understood?

648
00:49:39,206 --> 00:49:41,338
Her temper, honestly.

649
00:50:26,573 --> 00:50:29,048
Sherbet I made myself. Orange flavor.

650
00:50:29,713 --> 00:50:31,147
There's strawberry too.

651
00:50:32,813 --> 00:50:34,500
I like orange.

652
00:50:37,880 --> 00:50:41,171
I'm very curious about
why you were so sad,

653
00:50:41,807 --> 00:50:43,864
but you don't have to tell me
if you'd rather not.

654
00:50:51,913 --> 00:50:54,507
Want me to keep everyone out
so you can be alone?

655
00:50:57,694 --> 00:51:00,454
I'm so upset about Gyu O.

656
00:51:01,700 --> 00:51:04,266
I'm scared to death Gyu Rim will find out.

657
00:51:08,681 --> 00:51:12,054
Could you let me in on whatever it is?

658
00:51:14,461 --> 00:51:16,387
Do you remember what I said before?

659
00:51:16,906 --> 00:51:19,444
That I'm not taking Gyu Rim away from you.

660
00:51:19,847 --> 00:51:24,947
I'm coming to you
and becoming your big brother.

661
00:51:26,521 --> 00:51:29,056
Couldn't you think of me as a big brother,

662
00:51:29,324 --> 00:51:32,474
as family, and tell me?

663
00:51:42,371 --> 00:51:47,387
Gyu Seo took secret photos
of what was on Gyu O's phone.

664
00:51:52,075 --> 00:51:56,929
Gyu O is a host bar escort.

665
00:52:06,314 --> 00:52:08,164
He did it for the money.

666
00:52:09,254 --> 00:52:12,524
He had no choice. Medical bills
for the man he hurt.

667
00:52:14,187 --> 00:52:17,778
Gyu O always wanted
to be a police officer.

668
00:52:20,580 --> 00:52:24,465
I wanted to know who'd been squeezing
my brother for eight years,

669
00:52:25,531 --> 00:52:27,733
so on my way home from school,

670
00:52:27,927 --> 00:52:30,686
I went to the auto shop
where the man's wife supposedly works,

671
00:52:32,906 --> 00:52:34,902
and a guy working there said...

672
00:52:36,162 --> 00:52:39,572
the owner
and his wife get back tonight from Hawaii.

673
00:52:41,868 --> 00:52:44,886
Turns out she isn't staff.
She's the owner.

674
00:52:46,081 --> 00:52:50,586
He's such an idiot, played for a sucker
by con artists like that...

675
00:52:54,040 --> 00:52:59,022
But if I report it to the police,
Gyu O might get taken in too...

676
00:53:04,167 --> 00:53:05,800
Where is this place?

677
00:53:20,653 --> 00:53:22,120
Are you leaving the car with us?

678
00:53:22,160 --> 00:53:25,738
- Are you the owner?
- Yes, I'm the owner.

679
00:53:29,354 --> 00:53:31,856
Hey, I just got back.

680
00:53:34,402 --> 00:53:37,041
It rained all week and ruined everything.

681
00:53:37,066 --> 00:53:40,122
I don't think Hawaii and I get along.

682
00:53:43,001 --> 00:53:45,827
Sure, let's play a round next week.

683
00:53:45,941 --> 00:53:48,187
Yes, got it.

684
00:53:54,627 --> 00:53:57,593
Are you glaring at me right now?

685
00:54:01,294 --> 00:54:03,278
Is your husband's name Son Ji Yeol?

686
00:54:04,681 --> 00:54:07,163
- Who are you?
- Han Gyu O's brother.

687
00:54:07,973 --> 00:54:10,490
- Honey.
- Hey, sweetheart.

688
00:54:13,020 --> 00:54:15,631
- What? Who is this?
- Are you Son Ji Yeol?

689
00:54:17,148 --> 00:54:21,357
You said you needed more surgery,
but you look fine.

690
00:54:21,577 --> 00:54:23,333
And a trip to Hawaii, no less.

691
00:54:24,947 --> 00:54:26,307
Who are you?

692
00:54:26,833 --> 00:54:28,526
He says he's Han Gyu O's brother.

693
00:54:30,440 --> 00:54:32,386
I thought Gyu O didn't have a brother.

694
00:54:32,747 --> 00:54:36,440
How do you two take money
that ruined a man's life,

695
00:54:36,634 --> 00:54:38,698
and spend it on Hawaii and golf?

696
00:54:39,279 --> 00:54:42,429
We didn't pay for Hawaii
with Gyu O's money.

697
00:54:42,454 --> 00:54:44,006
Keep your mouth shut, ma'am.

698
00:54:48,659 --> 00:54:50,444
I'm still a patient.

699
00:54:50,565 --> 00:54:53,155
Because of Han Gyu O,
I'm still going to the hospital,

700
00:54:53,230 --> 00:54:57,082
and taking handfuls of pills.
For years now.

701
00:54:57,284 --> 00:54:58,855
You should have run into me instead.

702
00:55:00,559 --> 00:55:04,451
Trash like you should have run into me
so I could finish you properly.

703
00:55:04,953 --> 00:55:07,905
Excuse me, isn't that going
a little too far?

704
00:55:07,930 --> 00:55:10,283
I told you to shut your mouth, ma'am.

705
00:55:14,587 --> 00:55:17,972
From now on, I'm settling this
on Gyu O's behalf,

706
00:55:18,047 --> 00:55:21,148
so how you deceived
and threatened Han Gyu O,

707
00:55:21,494 --> 00:55:24,417
how you wrecked and mocked a man's life,

708
00:55:24,842 --> 00:55:27,558
I'll report every last detail, one by one,

709
00:55:27,999 --> 00:55:31,181
and you'd better hire
a very expensive, very good lawyer.

710
00:55:33,834 --> 00:55:35,795
Han Gyu O, that son of a...

711
00:55:36,807 --> 00:55:40,321
Eight years of bleeding money
and never once checking...

712
00:55:41,309 --> 00:55:43,109
who he's paying?

713
00:55:47,487 --> 00:55:49,274
You two have an accomplice, don't you?

714
00:56:03,940 --> 00:56:05,540
What do you think you're doing!

715
00:56:05,980 --> 00:56:09,084
What are you doing to my car?

716
00:56:09,109 --> 00:56:11,606
- Are you the host bar manager?
- Who are you?

717
00:56:13,086 --> 00:56:15,714
You know Han Gyu O, right?

718
00:56:17,481 --> 00:56:19,400
I hear you're the one who pulled him in.

719
00:56:20,274 --> 00:56:23,091
You worked with Son Ji Yeol,
feeding him lies about more surgery,

720
00:56:23,116 --> 00:56:25,213
and taking kickbacks for it.

721
00:56:27,550 --> 00:56:29,325
What are you talking about?

722
00:56:29,327 --> 00:56:31,313
Who's Son Ji Yeol? Who are you?

723
00:56:31,315 --> 00:56:33,619
Me? I'm Gyu O's brother.

724
00:56:34,314 --> 00:56:37,951
It means con artists like you...

725
00:56:38,247 --> 00:56:40,991
aren't playing Gyu O for a fool anymore.

726
00:56:42,887 --> 00:56:47,031
From this moment, lay one finger on Gyu O,

727
00:56:47,240 --> 00:56:51,125
and I'll kindly show you that living
is harder than dying.

728
00:56:59,634 --> 00:57:01,756
- Hello.
- How have you been?

729
00:57:01,757 --> 00:57:03,030
- Good.
- Is the manager in?

730
00:57:03,055 --> 00:57:05,384
They just stepped out,
but they'll be right back.

731
00:57:06,414 --> 00:57:08,143
I spoke with them this morning,

732
00:57:08,218 --> 00:57:10,399
and they said the Balmain
tailored set came in.

733
00:57:10,424 --> 00:57:11,505
The limited edition.

734
00:57:12,207 --> 00:57:15,635
- That just sold a moment ago.
- What?

735
00:57:16,587 --> 00:57:18,207
I said I'd buy it.

736
00:57:18,367 --> 00:57:21,532
You didn't state clearly
that you intended to purchase...

737
00:57:22,567 --> 00:57:26,608
I said I couldn't tell from photos,
so I'd come see it in person and buy it.

738
00:57:26,633 --> 00:57:30,576
I'm sorry. You didn't come, so we assumed
you weren't buying...

739
00:57:30,746 --> 00:57:34,113
- Ten minutes earlier and it'd be yours.
- What?

740
00:57:34,173 --> 00:57:37,376
It sold exactly ten minutes ago.

741
00:58:16,338 --> 00:58:19,939
- It's me. The freeloader.
- What?

742
00:58:21,773 --> 00:58:24,834
Why is a man like you wearing that?

743
00:58:24,867 --> 00:58:28,532
Why? A man like me can't wear this?

744
00:58:29,114 --> 00:58:31,159
That's insanely expensive.

745
00:58:31,953 --> 00:58:33,706
Did you steal Su Nam's card?

746
00:58:35,060 --> 00:58:36,821
I cashed out my savings for it. So what?

747
00:58:37,249 --> 00:58:38,886
I'll change out of it and come back,

748
00:58:38,914 --> 00:58:41,412
- so charge it to the card I gave you.
- Yes, sir.

749
00:58:41,437 --> 00:58:42,939
That's mine, that outfit.

750
00:58:43,741 --> 00:58:45,667
Seong Uk called dibs on it
as his birthday present.

751
00:58:45,687 --> 00:58:47,754
Dibs, my foot.

752
00:58:47,779 --> 00:58:50,473
Whoever pays first owns it. What of it?

753
00:58:50,827 --> 00:58:52,676
Don't be like that. Let me have it.

754
00:58:52,737 --> 00:58:54,100
You know what Seong Uk is like.

755
00:58:54,125 --> 00:58:55,942
He loses
it when he can't have what he wants.

756
00:58:55,967 --> 00:58:59,339
Whether he loses it
is none of my business.

757
00:59:02,631 --> 00:59:04,041
What do you think you're doing?

758
00:59:04,061 --> 00:59:06,959
- I'm licking it.
- Hey!

759
00:59:08,410 --> 00:59:11,467
I licked it and spat on it,
so it's mine now.

760
00:59:11,492 --> 00:59:14,214
You can't wear something
with someone's spit on it, right?

761
00:59:16,474 --> 00:59:19,717
It's fine. I'll dry-clean it.

762
00:59:23,453 --> 00:59:24,960
Hey!

763
00:59:29,986 --> 00:59:31,805
Smells amazing.

764
00:59:38,440 --> 00:59:40,626
I'll add ten percent. Sell it to me.

765
00:59:40,651 --> 00:59:42,071
No thanks.

766
00:59:42,606 --> 00:59:43,923
Twenty percent.

767
00:59:44,747 --> 00:59:48,014
Excuse me. I hear the meat here is famous,

768
00:59:48,182 --> 00:59:49,441
so what's the best thing on the menu?

769
00:59:49,466 --> 00:59:50,925
Everything here is good.

770
00:59:51,327 --> 00:59:53,554
This new one is good too. Give it a try.

771
00:59:53,727 --> 00:59:55,267
Just order a bit of everything.

772
00:59:55,281 --> 00:59:56,914
The more you order, the better the value.

773
00:59:56,939 --> 00:59:59,444
Is that so? Thank you.

774
00:59:59,954 --> 01:00:01,317
Twenty-two percent?

775
01:00:09,186 --> 01:00:12,766
If Seong Uk finds out you took it,
I'm dead.

776
01:00:12,791 --> 01:00:15,979
Save me, please. I'm begging you.

777
01:00:17,567 --> 01:00:19,180
Do ten bunny hops.

778
01:00:19,280 --> 01:00:21,867
Then I'll give you the outfit.

779
01:00:22,133 --> 01:00:24,479
You really have some nerve.

780
01:00:27,566 --> 01:00:29,899
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

781
01:00:40,013 --> 01:00:41,949
This is unbelievable.

782
01:00:42,291 --> 01:00:45,257
Want a bite? The meat melts in your mouth.

783
01:00:53,807 --> 01:00:55,794
Leaving? Take care.

784
01:01:07,948 --> 01:01:09,428
That's enough.

785
01:01:10,247 --> 01:01:12,016
You said ten.

786
01:01:12,626 --> 01:01:14,477
You don't have to do ten.

787
01:01:15,374 --> 01:01:16,610
Take it.

788
01:01:19,220 --> 01:01:20,864
Send me your account number by message.

789
01:01:23,420 --> 01:01:25,032
I don't need the money.

790
01:01:25,326 --> 01:01:29,108
Why would I take money from you,
when you'd sell your own life for money?

791
01:01:29,260 --> 01:01:31,948
You're ruining the taste. Go on, hurry up.

792
01:01:41,340 --> 01:01:42,946
Disgusting.

793
01:02:22,773 --> 01:02:26,598
Gyu Yeong must have packed up and left
while we were out.

794
01:02:29,167 --> 01:02:30,469
Does it hurt a lot?

795
01:02:41,443 --> 01:02:46,251
When things are hard, holding your hand
like this makes me feel so much better.

796
01:02:48,441 --> 01:02:51,854
Did something happen to you?

797
01:02:53,567 --> 01:02:55,748
No, it's just...

798
01:02:56,944 --> 01:02:58,809
I think I'll be fine by tomorrow.

799
01:03:00,344 --> 01:03:01,497
Look at this.

800
01:03:01,670 --> 01:03:03,857
Holding your hand already made it better.

801
01:03:10,753 --> 01:03:14,780
It makes me happy
to hold your hand too, Gyu Seo.

802
01:03:17,339 --> 01:03:21,274
Today was hard on me too,

803
01:03:22,739 --> 01:03:25,542
but thanks to you, I'm suddenly happy.

804
01:04:02,401 --> 01:04:04,648
I don't think we've met properly.

805
01:04:05,999 --> 01:04:07,113
No.

806
01:04:17,693 --> 01:04:19,221
Hello, Han Gyu O.

807
01:04:20,259 --> 01:04:22,741
I'm Kim Mu Jin, and as of today
I'm your big brother.

808
01:04:58,627 --> 01:05:00,933
(Love on the Menu)

809
01:05:00,989 --> 01:05:02,432
- You're hiding something from me.
- You're hiding something from me.

810
01:05:02,457 --> 01:05:04,183
Give me some time.

811
01:05:04,241 --> 01:05:05,381
What does that mean?

812
01:05:05,440 --> 01:05:07,222
What did our mother say she'd give you?

813
01:05:07,247 --> 01:05:08,494
I don't have a mother.

814
01:05:08,527 --> 01:05:09,721
- What?
- Why you...

815
01:05:09,746 --> 01:05:12,927
Fine, Han Gyu Yeong. You said
you tangle up your own life,

816
01:05:12,961 --> 01:05:14,721
so you and I are done here.

817
01:05:14,746 --> 01:05:17,515
I love not having my family
in front of me.

818
01:05:17,540 --> 01:05:19,530
Good thing you and I want the same thing.

819
01:05:19,557 --> 01:05:20,995
That Gyu Rim doesn't cry anymore.

820
01:05:21,020 --> 01:05:22,020
Hello?

821
01:05:22,045 --> 01:05:23,045
That she doesn't get hurt.

822
01:05:23,070 --> 01:05:26,069
- I'm not going to you.
- No.

823
01:05:26,507 --> 01:05:28,467
Shot down every day
and I come back every day.

824
01:05:28,513 --> 01:05:30,264
I'm not losing you again.

825
01:05:31,936 --> 01:05:33,736
Dramaday.me
